{"id":406,"date":"2020-09-22T15:57:54","date_gmt":"2020-09-22T15:57:54","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/?post_type=application&#038;p=406"},"modified":"2025-04-07T18:59:48","modified_gmt":"2025-04-07T18:59:48","slug":"masters-in-mathematical-sciences-application","status":"publish","type":"application","link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/application\/masters-in-mathematical-sciences-application\/","title":{"rendered":"Master&#8217;s in Mathematical Sciences Application"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-background-dim-30 page-cover\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#161228\"><\/span><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"2048\" height=\"2560\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-11978\" alt=\"\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-scaled.jpg\" style=\"object-position:60% 6%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"60% 6%\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-scaled.jpg 2048w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-240x300.jpg 240w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-819x1024.jpg 819w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-768x960.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-1229x1536.jpg 1229w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-1638x2048.jpg 1638w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-10x12.jpg 10w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 2048px) 100vw, 2048px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n<h1><\/h1>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"is-layout-flow wp-block-group pad-5\"><div class=\"wp-block-group__inner-container\">\n<h2>Overview<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-vivid-red-color has-text-color\"><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The&nbsp;<strong>AIMS Structured Master\u2019s Program<\/strong>&nbsp;runs over three semesters. The requisite skills phase of the AIMS course builds a standard core set of problem-solving skills: estimation, computation, approximation, modelling, data analysis and statistics. The elective review phase allows students to apply these skills in some of the most exciting areas of science.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>During the final phase of the AIMS course students do a research project and write a scientific report under the supervision of an expert researcher on a topic of their choice. Research initiated in these projects often develops into further postgraduate research work after AIMS.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Why Apply:<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<ol>\n<li>Classes are taught by renowned African and international lecturers, supported by a team of resident tutors.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Students and teachers live on campus to encourage a 24-hour learning environment.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>A highly interactive teaching environment where students are encouraged to learn together through questions and discoveries.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>An emphasis on programming and scientific computing with 24-hour access to computer rooms and the internet.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>A diverse Pan-African student body from across Africa.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>AIMS graduates are highly employable and embark on outstanding graduate programs and professional careers in Africa and around the world.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Full scholarships will be awarded to all accepted students of the Structured Master&#8217;s Degree Program, with facilities including accommodation, food and health insurance.<\/li>\n<\/ol>\n\n\n\n<h2>Application Instructions:<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<h2>Visit the <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https:\/\/apply.aims-network.org\/\" target=\"_blank\">LINK<\/a>&nbsp;to apply for the AIMS Master\u2019s Programs<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Application Documents<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Applicants must hold or expect to obtain by the date of commencement of AIMS training, either of the following in mathematics or any other science\/engineering discipline with a significant mathematics component:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>a) a four-year undergraduate degree in mathematics or any science\/ engineering discipline.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>b) a three-year undergraduate degree with an honours in mathematics or any science\/ engineering discipline.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>c) a three-year undergraduate degree with GCE A-level or Baccalaureat by August 2024 (only for AIMS-Ghana and AIMS-Rwanda).<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Candidate records must also demonstrate leadership and community service skills.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Women are strongly encouraged to apply.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"white-text has-white-color has-text-color\"><a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/master-of-mathematical-sciences\/\" target=\"_blank\">More on Regular Master&#8217;s Program<\/a><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"has-white-color has-text-color\"><a href=\"https:\/\/nexteinstein.org\/academic_program\/aims-co-operative-masters-program\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">More on CO-OP Master&#8217;s Program<\/a><\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-white-color has-text-color\"><\/p>\n<\/div><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover is-light has-background-dim-70 app-cover\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-background-dim\" style=\"background-color:#161228\"><\/span><img decoding=\"async\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-10000040\" alt=\"\" src=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story.jpg\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" srcset=\"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story.jpg 1600w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story-300x200.jpg 300w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story-1024x683.jpg 1024w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story-768x512.jpg 768w, https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/2020\/09\/African-Institute-for-Mathematical-Sciences-AIMS-Our-story-1536x1024.jpg 1536w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 1600px) 100vw, 1600px\" \/><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container\">\n<h3 class=\"white-text has-white-color has-text-color\">      Application Deadline: 31st March 2025<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<div style=\"height:45px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"white-text has-white-color has-text-color\"><\/h3>\n<\/div><\/div>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Overview The&nbsp;AIMS Structured Master\u2019s Program&nbsp;runs over three semesters. The requisite skills phase of the AIMS course builds a standard core set of problem-solving skills: estimation, computation, approximation, modelling, data analysis and statistics. The elective review phase allows students to apply these skills in some of the most exciting areas of science. During the final phase<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":11978,"parent":0,"template":"","meta":{"advgb_blocks_editor_width":"","advgb_blocks_columns_visual_guide":""},"tags":[],"acf":[],"featured_img":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/wp-content\/uploads\/sites\/4\/2020\/09\/MASTERS-IN-MATHEMATICAL-SCIENCE-Application-English-scaled.jpg","coauthors":[],"author_meta":{"author_link":"https:\/\/aims.edu.gh\/author\/chris\/","display_name":"chris"},"relative_dates":{"created":"Posted 5 years ago","modified":"Updated 8